## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design privacy-preserving cross-tenant ML pipelines with real-time inference, deployment discipline, and enterprise-grade governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation and differential privacy for cross-tenant insights
- Per-tenant feature stores with isolated data domains
- Vertex AI canary deployments with traffic splitting
- Real-time endpoints with autoscaling and cost budget controls
- Data lineage tracking in Data Catalog
- Drift monitoring (CTR) and latency SLAs logged to BigQuery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vertex AI Canary Rollout Configuration
const canaryDeployment = {
  endpoint: {
    displayName: 'ad-click-prediction-endpoint',
    model: 'ad-click-model-v1',
    trafficSplit: { '0': 20, '1': 80 } // 20% canary, 80% production
  },
  monitoring: {
    driftThresholds: { ctr: 0.05 },
    latencyThresholds: { p99: 200 },
    alertBudgetPercent: 80
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes how a candidate designs a privacy-conscious, multi-tenant ML pipeline on GCP, balancing data governance, per-tenant isolation, cost, and operability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation with per-tenant datasets and Feature Store
- PII de-identification in Dataflow
- Canary deployments and traffic shifting
- Drift detection and Explainable AI for governance
- Privacy logging and rollback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: shift partial traffic to canary on drift alert
function rollbackOnDrift(isDrift, canaryEndpoint, prodEndpoint){
  if(!isDrift) return;
  // gradually shift traffic back to prod
  setTraffic(canaryEndpoint, 0.0);
  setTraffic(prodEndpoint, 1.0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding with data retention?
- How would you scale feature store lookups for thousands of tenants?
